From 20a869bdbd30966333130f5fb5a83157acfee885 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Rowland <simon@simonrowland.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:54:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Fix THERMOCALC aMgO by storing the periclase reference energy

compute_activities() initialises G0_per to 0. The tc branch calls
G_EM_function(..., "per", ...) and never copies PP_db.gbase, so

    system_aMgO = exp(Gamma_MgO / RT)

which is about 1e-21 at 1873 K. The sb branch does assign gbase,
and divides by 4 for EM_database 1 and 2 (the 4-cation Mg4O4
end-member). That sb assignment is unchanged.

The other tc oxide references store PP_db.gbase with no extra
scaling. Al2O3, TiO2 and H2O assign gbase after the research-group
branch. The tc SiO2 branch assigns quartz and coesite gbase inside
the branch. The factor multiply is commented out on every one of
those assignments, and none of them applies the sb /4. The tc MgO
fix is the same store of PP_db.gbase, with no factor and no /4.

Repro on v1.9.6, --db=ig, --Temp=1599.85 C (1873.00 K),
    --buffer=qfm --buffer_n=-3.205734 (log10 fO2 = -8). R = 0.0083144
kJ/mol/K, the value initialise sets. Printed Gamma and gbase are
in kJ despite the Gamma[J] heading.

Kume 2000 Table 4 sample 305, wt% SiO2 34.6, Al2O3 39, CaO 19.6,
MgO 6.8, Pres=1e-9 kbar (1e-6 bar):
  before aMgO = 1.568821e-21 = exp(Gamma_MgO/RT)
  after  aMgO = 5.679362e-01
  Gamma_MgO = -746.00224 kJ, G_per = -737.19195 kJ
  exp((Gamma_MgO - G_per)/RT) = 0.567936
  aSiO2 = 4.556864e-02 and aAl2O3 = 1.000000e+00 unchanged
  assemblage unchanged: fsp 0.18391, liq 0.50317, cpx 0.11432,
  cor 0.19860, status 0

Same bulk at Pres=0.001 kbar (1 bar):
  before aMgO = 1.287131e-21, after 4.659243e-01
  aSiO2 = 1.960119e-02 and aAl2O3 = 1 unchanged
  assemblage unchanged (fsp, cpx, liq, liq, ne, cor)

Periclase-saturated Fe-free bulk, wt% SiO2 25, Al2O3 10, CaO 15,
MgO 50, 1e-6 bar, assemblage liq + fper:
  before aMgO = 2.761891e-21, after 9.998449e-01
  aSiO2 and aAl2O3 unchanged

The FeO reference is not changed. On the sb path G0_fper is
divided by 4 for EM_database 1 and 2 and then overwritten by
PP_db.gbase. That overwrite is left for upstream to confirm.
---
 src/toolkit.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/toolkit.c b/src/toolkit.c
index 8ff080f..49281e4 100644
--- a/src/toolkit.c
+++ b/src/toolkit.c
@@ -2006,6 +2006,10 @@ global_variable compute_activities(			int					 EM_database,
 		double G0_per = 0.0;
 		if (strcmp(gv.research_group, "tc") 	== 0 ){
 			PP_db  			= G_EM_function(gv.research_group, gv.EM_dataset, gv.len_ox,z_b.id,z_b.bulk_rock, z_b.apo, z_b.P, z_b.T , "per", "equilibrium");
+			/* tc oxide references store gbase with no factor and no /4.
+			   Al2O3, TiO2, H2O and the tc SiO2 branch do the same.
+			   G0_per stayed 0 here, so aMgO was exp(Gamma_MgO/RT). */
+			G0_per 			= PP_db.gbase;
 		}
 		else if (strcmp(gv.research_group, "sb") 	== 0 ){
 			PP_db  			= G_EM_function(gv.research_group, gv.EM_dataset, gv.len_ox,z_b.id,z_b.bulk_rock, z_b.apo, z_b.P, z_b.T , "pe", "equilibrium");
